id: pm-x710qm
title: "Four read surfaces publish a jq_selector that is guaranteed to return nothing: the self-describing row contract is present, vacuous, and indistinguishable from an empty result"
description: "deps, stats, aggregate and get emit the universal jq_selector with row_keys empty, so the documented extraction one-liner silently yields zero rows on surfaces that demonstrably have rows."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ergonomics,composability,contracts,pm-cli,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:03:48.007Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:57.469Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:05.236Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:05.236Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: No read surface publishes a jq_selector that cannot return the rows its envelope contains; Surfaces with row collections populate row_keys with the real key names even when --fields is unsupported; A gate evaluates each read command envelope against its own published selector and asserts the returned row count matches the envelope contents; Surfaces that emit no envelope at all (the NDJSON event stream) are declared as such in the contract documentation rather than discovered by a parser returning null
value: "Makes the one published extraction expression trustworthy, which is the precondition for every shell and jq workflow the product advertises."
why_now: The composability principle promises grep/jq pipelines; a contract that lies by returning empty is worse for a scripted agent than no contract at all.
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: Implemented truthful collection and no-row contracts with nested-path jq selection; validated every published selector against real envelopes.
expected_result: "If a read surface publishes jq_selector, evaluating it returns the rows the envelope contains."
actual_result: "deps (18 edges), stats, aggregate and get publish the selector with row_keys empty; it returns zero rows on all four."
component: cli/read-surfaces
