close_reason: "Delivered truthful universal SDK/CLI read-row contracts, nested path extraction, scalar/no-row semantics, real jq conformance, packed-consumer acceptance, and complete release-gate evidence."
body: "## Measured 2026-07-31 at HEAD across nineteen read surfaces\n\nThe published extraction contract is `.row_contract.jq_selector`, whose value on every surface that emits it is:\n\n```\n.row_contract.row_keys[] as $key | .[$key][]?\n```\n\nThat expression is a pure function of `row_keys`. When `row_keys` is empty or absent, it yields nothing — always, regardless of what the envelope actually contains.\n\n| class | surfaces | count |\n|---|---|---|\n| contract usable (`row_keys` populated) | list, search, history, activity, health, next, context | 7 |\n| contract present but vacuous (`row_keys: []` or absent, selector still published) | deps, stats, aggregate, get | 4 |\n| no `row_contract` at all | comments, notes, files, docs, graph, contracts, validate | 7 |\n| no envelope (NDJSON stream, no contract possible) | events | 1 |\n\n## The defect this item owns\n\nThe middle class. `pm deps pm-doxj --json` emits:\n\n```\n\"row_contract\": {\"command\":\"deps\",\"row_keys\":[],\"fields\":\"unsupported\",\n                 \"jq_selector\":\".row_contract.row_keys[] as $key | .[$key][]?\"}\n```\n\nThe item has 18 dependency edges. The published selector returns zero rows. `pm stats --json` behaves identically while carrying `by_type` and `by_status` collections.\n\nA missing contract fails loudly: the agent sees `null`, knows the surface is not covered, and special-cases it. A vacuous contract fails silently: the agent runs the documented one-liner, gets an empty stream, and cannot distinguish \"this surface never populates row_keys\" from \"the query matched nothing\". Silence is the worse failure because it is indistinguishable from a legitimate empty result, and every downstream count, loop and guard reads zero.\n\n## Relationship to the general row-contract programme\n\n`pm-sb0tns` owns the general problem — that no single shell or jq expression works across pm — and its acceptance criteria already require a documented one-liner exercised by a test, and require surfaces that cannot project fields to state why. This item is the narrow, immediately fixable subset: a surface that declares `fields: \"unsupported\"` and carries no row keys must not also publish a selector that is guaranteed to return nothing. Either it names its real row collection, or it omits `jq_selector` so the absence is visible.\n\nThis is not a request to make every surface projectable. It is a request that the self-describing contract never describe itself falsely.\n\n## Minimal correct shape\n\n- A surface that has row collections populates `row_keys` with their real key names, even when `--fields` is unsupported. `deps` has `nodes` and `edges`; `stats` has its count maps; `aggregate` has its groups.\n- A surface with genuinely no row collection omits `jq_selector` entirely, or sets it to a value the contract defines as \"no rows on this surface\".\n- A gate asserts the invariant directly: for every read command, if `row_contract.jq_selector` is present then evaluating it against the same envelope must return the same row count the envelope actually contains. That is checkable without knowing anything about the individual command."
